// A concrete type error inside a generic body NOBODY instantiates is still an error.
// `analyze()` IS `emit()`, and the emit walk used to skip a template body entirely, so this built clean —
// which is worst for a package author: ship `check`-green, and every consumer gets the error instead.
// `checkUninstantiatedTemplates` walks the body once with `T` left symbolic; the `int32` line mentions no
// type parameter, so the ordinary rule sees it.
fn void neverCalled<T>(T unused) {
    int32 x = "not an int";      // ERROR: no implicit conversion, and this is concrete
}
fn int32 main() { return 0; }
